ALVA — Full Control / Move Codename Refactor

Work directly in the current Alva repository and perform a complete, behavior-preserving refactor of the gameplay control/action/move codenames.

Before editing, inspect the existing architecture and follow the established data-driven design. This is a browser-based 2D Canvas fighting game with no build framework. The relevant systems currently span at least:

* js/config.js
* js/core/input-manager.js
* js/game/touch-controls.js
* js/game/fighter-controller.js
* js/game/character.js
* js/game/combat.js
* js/game/combat-ai.js
* js/game/arena.js
* js/game/fighter-status.js
* js/game/clone.js
* js/game/charged-technique.js
* js/data/characters.js
* js/ui/mobile-abilities.js
* gameplay tests under tests/
* README.md
* ALVA_SPEC.md
* any other file discovered by repository-wide search

The objective is naming only. Do not rebalance, redesign, simplify, or otherwise alter gameplay.

Canonical new names

Use these exact code-facing names.

Concept	Canonical codename
Run left	runLeft
Run right	runRight
Dedicated movement/dash left request	mouvementLeft
Dedicated movement/dash right request	mouvementRight
Basic Attack 1	ba1
Mid-air Basic Attack 1	maba1
Charged Basic Attack 1	cba1
Basic Attack 2	ba2
Mid-air Basic Attack 2	maba2
Charged Basic Attack 2	cba2
Jump	jump
Defense / Shield button	shield
Throw / unique basic attack	uniqueba
Special	transform
Charge button	charge
Pause	pause

Important: mouvement is intentionally spelled exactly that way. Do not “correct” it to movement.

Also, do not rename the existing movement character tuning/config object. For example, def.movement.dashSpeed, acceleration, air movement, etc. stay under movement. The mouvementLeft / mouvementRight names are specifically control codenames.

