Unique basic attack

The current Throw button/action uses the generic input primary and the attack ID throw.

Replace the button/action codename with:

uniqueba

The code-facing move ID should also use uniqueba where practical so there is one canonical identity.

The move is still visually/mechanically #0001’s shuriken throw.

Do not rename sprite files just for this refactor. Existing throw1, throw2, throw3, shuriken sprites, etc. may remain as asset filenames.

Do not change:

* projectile timing;
* projectile speed;
* damage;
* Launch behavior;
* release frame;
* cooldown;
* ground-only restriction;
* collision behavior.

The mobile button may continue to display the character-specific Shuriken icon/name. uniqueba is the code identifier, not necessarily the visible label.

Shield

Replace the gameplay input codename:

defense -> shield

and:

defensePressed -> shieldPressed

Touch controls, keyboard bindings, gamepad bindings, Fighter input reads, AI output, test fixtures, etc. must use shield.

Preserve the Shield mechanic completely:

* held input;
* ground and mid-air shield behavior;
* perfect Shield;
* Energy cost on blocks;
* exhaustion behavior;
* blockstun;
* artwork;
* shield FX;
* attack buffering while Shield is held.

Do not blindly rename unrelated generic engine abstractions simply because they contain the word “defense.” The goal is canonical button/action/move codenames, not an unrelated architectural rewrite.

